---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="SecOps-NG — Sovereign Security for the EU">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">A digital-sovereignty collective</span>
      <h1>Sovereign security, built in the open, for the Europe we want to keep.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We are a collective of practitioners building durable, agentic security
        operations on sovereign European infrastructure. Our work is aimed
        squarely at the mid-size organizations who carry the continent's
        economy — and who face the <strong>NIS2 deadline in July 2026</strong>
        without the budgets of the Fortune 500 or the comfort of dependence on
        foreign hyperscalers.
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        This is not a product. It is a federation, a commons, and an invitation.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/secops-ng" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Contribute on GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/about">Read the manifesto</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pillars">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Three pillars</span>
      <h2>What the collective is building.</h2>
      <div class="pillar-grid">
        <article class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-num">01</div>
          <h3>Sovereign Infrastructure</h3>
          <p>
            Security workloads run on EU-operated, EU-governed compute. We
            build on <a href="https://nebul.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Nebul</a>
            and other sovereign clouds so that data, telemetry, and response
            stay inside European jurisdiction — by architecture, not by promise.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-num">02</div>
          <h3>Durable Workflows</h3>
          <p>
            Incident response is too important to rely on best-effort scripts.
            We orchestrate detection, triage, and remediation as
            <a href="https://temporal.io" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Temporal.io</a>
            workflows — replayable, auditable, and resilient to the chaos of
            real-world breaches.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar">
          <div class="pillar-num">03</div>
          <h3>Open Framework</h3>
          <p>
            Agentic SecOps belongs in the commons. Our playbooks, agents, and
            reference architectures are open-source so any community can read
            them, audit them, fork them, and improve them. Sovereignty without
            transparency is just a different cage.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="join">
    <div class="container join-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Join the collective</span>
      <h2>Federations beat monopolies. Help us build one.</h2>
      <p>
        We are looking for security engineers, SREs, policy folks, lawyers,
        translators, designers, and anyone who believes Europe deserves
        defenses it owns. The work is happening in the open — repositories,
        issues, design discussions, and manuals are all on GitHub.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/secops-ng" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Join the conversation on GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/blog">Read the manuals</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero {
      padding: 5rem 0 3rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .lede {
      max-width: 44rem;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .pillars { padding: 4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .pillar-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    .pillar {
      padding: 1.5rem;
      background: var(--paper-soft);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .pillar-num {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .join { padding: 4rem 0 2rem; }
    .join-inner { max-width: 44rem; }
  </style>
</Base>
